; shl_amount_at_or_above_word_size: a shift count of 64 or more is out of
; range.
;
; The VM guards the amount with `(0..64)` before shifting. A VM that
; computes in unbounded integers would let `PUSH 1 / PUSH 64 / SHL` reach
; the push check and raise ARITHMETIC_OVERFLOW instead of INVALID_SHIFT --
; a fault-identity error -- while `PUSH 0 / PUSH 100 / SHL` would complete
; and push 0, a fault-versus-success error on a verifier-clean
; four-instruction program. Both are admissible to a stored program, so
; both are reachable from a signed account.

PUSH 1
PUSH 64
SHL
HALT
